# Uploaded content (local storage backend's on-disk save location - see
# storage.py). Real, potentially large user-uploaded files don't belong
# in git; a few had ended up committed here before this rule existed -
# see `git log --all --full-history -- server/uploads` if that history
# ever needs clearing out with a filter-repo pass. Covers the "test
# report" case too (server/report_uploads/, previously listed alone).
server/uploads/
server/report_uploads/
server/fellow_uploads/

# git-format-patch output - these are meant to be shared/applied
# elsewhere, not committed into the repo itself. Two had ended up
# tracked (0001-...patch, 0002-...patch, from a "package as patch"
# request that got committed by mistake) - removed from tracking
# alongside this rule; see git log if that history needs revisiting.
*.patch